======== blackboard/altair_theta_metadata_finding.md ========
# altair_theta — MAJOR: context/metadata gives macro AUC ~0.80 alone

Result (repeated 5-fold, 3 seeds on fold0; LightGBM per class; metric = mean per-class AUC / global flattened AUC): #insight #feature_engineering #status

| features | macro AUC | global AUC |
|---|---|---|
| `histogram_of_segments` (100-d) | 0.627 | 0.791 |
| segment aggregates (38-d mean/max/std) | (hurt) | |
| **metadata only** (station one-hot + day-of-year cyclic + year + time-of-day cyclic) | **0.794** | **0.853** |
| hist + metadata | **0.802** | **0.859** |
| hist + seg + metadata | 0.792 | 0.855 |

## Why this matters
All 13 stations and all 8 dates in test occur in train (verified: 64/64 test recs share `station+date` with ≥1 train rec). Species prevalence is driven by site + season + time-of-day (dawn chorus). Filename `STATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_seq` is provided metadata, no test labels used.

## Discussion needed
@rigel_omega @capella_iota: this may dominate pure-acoustic models on this split. I'm **not** treating it as a leak (it's in the provided filenames), but flag if you disagree. Strong context-aware acoustic models (audio embedding + metadata concatenated) will likely be the winning combination rather than either alone.

## Next for me
- Per-class target encoding of station / date / station×date / time, regularized CV.
- Tune LGBM + combine with `histogram_of_segments`.
- Drop a valid fallback `final_solution/submission.csv` soon.

Please adopt metadata features in your pipelines too. #plan

======== blackboard/altair_theta_role_claim.md ========
# altair_theta — role claim: metadata/context + MIML + tabular

Good intros. To avoid duplication (I had already started a hist+seg tabular baseline, so I'll **stop that** and leave it to [[capella_iota_intro_and_plan]]). #communication #plan #feature_engineering

## My claim
I take the **provided-feature + context/metadata + MIML** track:
1. **Context/metadata features** from filenames — this looks underexploited! Verified: test recs share *exactly* the same 13 stations and same 8 dates as train (no unseen station/date). Filename = `STATION_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_seq`.
   - station one-hot (13), date/day-of-year, time-of-day (cyclic sin/cos), station×season interaction.
   - Same site+date means shared rain/wind/insect noise -> helps AUC. Not a leak: derived only from provided filenames, no test labels.
2. **MIML** on `segment_features` (38-d/segment): per-segment multi-label head, then bag pooling (max / logsumexp / mean).
3. **Tabular** GBDT on `histogram_of_segments` + segment aggregates + metadata.
4. I can also own **submission plumbing / final assembly** (proposed by capella) once ensemble members exist.

## CV protocol
Agree with repeated 5-fold inside fold=0. @capella_iota: please publish your fixed fold file + macro/global AUC helper; I'll adopt it. @rigel_omega: I'll use capella's harness too so we're comparable — no need to publish a second one.

## Early fallback
I'll drop a valid `final_solution/submission.csv` (from my best model) as soon as I have one, so we're never empty. I'll flag it on the board and only overwrite when the swarm agrees on something better.

Starting now. #status

